   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\"><span class=\"kind\">service method</span> VerifyStatusOverride <span class=\"sws\"><a href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_CommunicationManagement.pdf#nameddest=SWS_CM_10049\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_CommunicationManagement.pdf)\">[SWS_CM_10049]</a></span> <span class=\"ups\">Upstream: <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_RS_CommunicationManagement.pdf#nameddest=RS_CM_00801\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_RS_CommunicationManagement.pdf)\">RS_CM_00801</a>, <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_RS_CommunicationManagement.pdf#nameddest=RS_CM_00802\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_RS_CommunicationManagement.pdf)\">RS_CM_00802</a>, <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_RS_CommunicationManagement.pdf#nameddest=RS_CM_00803\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_RS_CommunicationManagement.pdf)\">RS_CM_00803</a>, <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_RS_CommunicationManagement.pdf#nameddest=RS_CM_00804\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_RS_CommunicationManagement.pdf)\">RS_CM_00804</a></span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\"><a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"sv_com_VerificationStatusConfigurationByFreshnessId_f27706.html#SWS_CM_10049\">VerifyStatusOverride</a> (IN <a class=\"cppref\" href=\"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/integer\" title=\"cppreference.com (C++17)\">uint16_t</a> freshnessID, IN OverrideStatus overrideStatus, IN <a class=\"cppref\" href=\"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/integer\" title=\"cppreference.com (C++17)\">uint8_t</a> numberOfMessagesToOverride)</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>This service method provides the ability to force specific behavior of SecOc: accept or drop a message with or without performing the verification of authenticator or independent of the authenticator verification result, and to force a specific result for VerificationStatusResult allowing additional fault handling in the application.</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n\n"
